      "rev_n_21_d5cb8f_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_21_d5cb8f_0",
        "node_id": "n_21_d5cb8f",
        "thought_text": "Since the constraints allow O(N) or O(N log N), a brute-force simulation checking every possible K from 1 to 100,000 is acceptable but inefficient. However, we can optimize this by noting that the answer only changes when K crosses a value present in the input array. We can iterate through the sorted unique values of d_i, determining the number of ABCs and ARCs for K = d_i + 1, and check if the condition holds, effectively reducing the search space to the number of unique elements.",
